  "data": {
    "body": "Let $A$ be an $m \\times n$ matrix and $\\mathbf{b}$ be a non-zero vector in $\\mathbb{R}^{m}$. Which of the following statements must be TRUE?\n\n(i) If $A \\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the trivial solution, then $A \\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ has no solution.\n\n(ii) If $A \\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ has exactly one solution, then $A$ is an $m \\times n$ matrix with $m \\geq n$.\n\n(iii) If $A \\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ has infinitely many solutions, then $A \\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n(iv) If $A$ is an $n \\times n$ square matrix, then $A \\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ has exactly one solution.",
